{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1331283-helping-to-flesh-out-a-character","id":1331283,"title":"Helping to flesh out a character","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2019-08-16T19:42:34-07:00","id":1331283,"title":"Helping to flesh out a character","content":"<span style=\"color:#1A1A1B\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">A NWO spook who fucked up one too many times. Impulsive. Sent to rot in a hell hole.</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#1A1A1B\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Detective in a noir film.</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#1A1A1B\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Enhanced aiming and skill in firearms, including gun fu. And deadly martial arts.</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#1A1A1B\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Someone capable of matching Sherlock Holmes and carry out the work of entire teams of analysts (figure out who a serial killer is from the location of his murders). Includes lie detector skills and good luck.<br /> <br /> He's got low level enhancements from a time in Iteration X/ Progenitors when he started to learn Time. Smarter, stronger, faster, with less exhaustion. But what's the kind that's low maintenance and not visible? <br /> <br /> What spheres does he have, and what kind of augmentations? </span></span></span><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-08-16T20:10:55-07:00","id":1331287,"title":"","content":"Nanomachines and certain muscle augmentations are low maintenance, I think the old progeniter (Maybe new as well idk) books have a few augmentations that literally run off of your metabolism and they run perfectly fine as long as you eat an extra 500 calories or so every day.<br /> <br /> It also depends on if we are using 'normal ass mage creation' but<br /> <br /> Spheres:<br /> NWO's whole deal is Mind, so that. Entropy would be needed if you wanted to tell someone is lying without mind 2.<br /> Life/Matter/Time from Prog/It X<br /> Forces or just using more Life if you want to be able to kung-fu kick someones chest off. Forces lets you do this with super fancy bullets.<br /> <br /> Augments: There's a nice nanomachines in the skin augment that gives you a real nice armor and I think it lets you regen, but it doesn't do well with other augmentations but serves real well if thats your only one.<br /> Outside of that you have the regular 'replace my muscles with machines' upgrade that makes you far above human, and then the even more vulgar 'replace my bones and most of me with metal' so you can hit as hard as a truck<br /> The latter doesn't sound like it fits very well though unless you want to recreate the scene in Twilight where you stop a car dramatically to save -love interest-<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25315-jihelu","name":"Jihelu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"167"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}